hadiths[9]{hadithnumber,text}:
"254","How much is the blood-money: al-Haytham ibn Khalid al-Juhani narrated to us, Waki narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Makhul, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died while the blood-money was eight hundred dinars, then Umar after him feared, so he made it twelve thousand dirhams or one thousand dinars."
"255","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Husayn narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb: that the value of the blood-money in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was eight hundred dinars."
"256","Wahb ibn Bayan, Ibn al-Sarh, and Ahmad ibn Sa'id said: Ibn Wahb informed us, Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, who said: I read in the letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to Amr ibn Hazm when he sent him to Najran - and the letter was with Abu Bakr ibn Hazm - the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote in it: This is an exposition from Allah and His Messenger: (O you who believe, fulfill contracts). And he wrote verses from it until he reached: (Indeed Allah is swift in reckoning). Then he wrote: This is the book of wounds: For a life, one hundred camels; for the nose when its severing is complete, one hundred camels; for the eye, fifty camels; for the ear, fifty camels; for the hand, fifty camels; for the foot, fifty camels; for every finger of those, ten camels; for the ma'mumah (wound reaching the brain membrane), a third of a life; for the ja'ifah (piercing wound), a third of a life; for the munaqqilah (bone-displacing fracture), fifteen; for the mudihah (bone-exposing wound), five camels; and for a tooth, five camels. Ibn Shihab said: This is what I read in the letter the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote, which was with Abu Bakr ibn Hazm. Abu Dawud said: This has been transmitted with a connected chain but is not sound; Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated it from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from his father, from his grandfather."
"257","Abu Hubayrah narrated to us, who said: I read it in the original of Yahya ibn Hamzah; Sulayman ibn Arqam narrated to me. And Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us; my father and my uncle narrated to me, both saying: Yahya ibn Hamzah, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, likewise. Abu Dawud said: What Sulayman ibn Dawud said, he erred in."
"258","al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Dawud [al-Khawlani - trustworthy -], from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from his father, from his grandfather; al-Hakam erred in it."
"259","Musa ibn Isma'il narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Amr ibn Hazm, who said: In the letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - meaning this one - was: For the male organ, the blood-money; and for the tongue, the blood-money."
"260","Musa narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Makhul, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the tongue, the blood-money; for the male organ, the blood-money; and for the front teeth, five obligations each."
"261","Muhammad ibn [Abdullah] narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Maghra, narrated to us, Muhammad, meaning Ibn Ishaq, narrated to us. I heard Makhul saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed the blood-money for the two testicles."
"262","Qutaybah narrated to us, al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn al-Had, from Ibn Shihab, who said: [The Messenger of Allah] (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the spine, the blood-money."
